; GENERATED by packages/tscaly/tools/genunicodeprops.py. Do not edit; edit the
; generator. Regenerate after a submodule pin bump.
;
; ★ THE CANONICAL PROPERTY NAME IS AN INT. The reference maps an alias to a
; canonical NAME and then uses that name as the key of the value tables, so the
; string is an identity and never a text. 1 = General_Category, 2 = Script,
; 3 = Script_Extensions, 0 = not a non-binary property — which is the value the
; reference spells as the empty string, and the one `scanCharacterClassEscape`
; branches on.
;
; ★ Script_Extensions shares Script's value set, and the reference says why: a
; character's Script_Extensions is one or more Script values, and a property
; value expression admits exactly one — so the two sets are the same set.
;
; ★ NO `use` CLAUSE. A cross-module free function of this package resolves
; unqualified — Keywords.get_identifier_token is the precedent, and the scanner
; has called it without one since slice 3 — and an explicit `use` changes the
; MANGLED NAME at the call site while leaving the definition unqualified, which
; links as an undefined symbol rather than as a diagnostic (root CLAUDE.md: a
; `use` line feeds the call-mangling machinery, not only visibility).


; Table 66: the non-binary property aliases and their canonical names.
; https://tc39.es/ecma262/#table-nonbinary-unicode-properties
function non_binary_unicode_property(s: Slice[char]) returns int
{
    if s.length = 2
    {
        if kw_eq(s.data, Slice[char](2, "gc"))
            return 1
        if kw_eq(s.data, Slice[char](2, "sc"))
            return 2
    }
    if s.length = 3
    {
        if kw_eq(s.data, Slice[char](3, "scx"))
            return 3
    }
    if s.length = 6
    {
        if kw_eq(s.data, Slice[char](6, "Script"))
            return 2
    }
    if s.length = 16
    {
        if kw_eq(s.data, Slice[char](16, "General_Category"))
            return 1
    }
    if s.length = 17
    {
        if kw_eq(s.data, Slice[char](17, "Script_Extensions"))
            return 3
    }
    0
}

